  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA consisting of NNN integers - A1,A2,⋯ ,ANA_1, A_2, \\cdots, A_NA1​,A2​,⋯,AN​. For each index iii find the maximum number of inversions in the entire array you can get by changing this element to any real\\textbf{real}real number.\n\nNote: The number of inversions in an array AAA is the number of pairs of indices iii, jjj such that 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i &lt; j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N and Ai&gt;AjA_i &gt; A_jAi​&gt;Aj​\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of 2 lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN  — the size of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space separated integers denoting the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, NNN space separated integers where the ithi^{th}ith integer denotes the answer for the ithi^{th}ith index of the array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤3⋅105",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (18 points):**",
      "1≤N≤1501 \\leq N \\leq 1501≤N≤150",
      "The sum of NNN across all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1042 \\cdot 10^42⋅104",
      "There are at most 50 tests with N&gt;10N&gt;10N&gt;10 and there is at most 1 test with N&gt;50N&gt;50N&gt;50.",
      "**Subtask 2 (22 points):**",
      "1≤N≤10001 \\leq N \\leq 10001≤N≤1000",
      "The sum of NNN across all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1032 \\cdot 10^32⋅103.",
      "**Subtask 3 (60 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2\n1 2\n4\n4 8 6 2",
        "output": "1 1 \n6 4 5 4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTestcase 1: The initial array is [1,2][1, 2][1,2].\n\nLet us now try to modify A1A_1A1​ to get the maximum number of inversions. We can set A1=3A_1 = 3A1​=3, and the new array [3,2][3, 2][3,2] has 1 inversion. \nWe can show that this is the maximum number of inversions we can achieve by modifying A1A_1A1​, and so the first output is 111.\nLet us now try to modify A2A_2A2​ to get the maximum number of inversions. We can set A2=0.5A_2 = 0.5A2​=0.5, and the new array [1,0.5][1, 0.5][1,0.5] has 1 inversion. \nWe can show that this is the maximum number of inversions we can achieve by modifying A2A_2A2​, and so the second output is 111."
      }
    ]
